---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import ComparisonTable from "~/components/illustration-kit/ComparisonTable.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="protagoras-euathlus"
  lead="The judgment and the contract seem to give opposite answers, whichever way the court rules."
>
  <ComparisonTable
    caption="What each possible ruling seems to imply"
    columns={["If the court…", "The judgment says", "The contract says"]}
    rows={[
      ["Rules for Protagoras", "Euathlus must pay now", "Euathlus has not yet won a case"],
      [
        "Rules for Euathlus",
        "Euathlus need not pay in this suit",
        "His first win has now occurred",
      ],
    ]}
  />
  <Panel title="Keep the two lawsuits separate" accent="blue">
    <p class="text-base">
      <strong>First lawsuit:</strong> Euathlus has not yet won a case when Protagoras sues. The
      fee is not due, so Euathlus wins.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-base">
      <strong>Possible second lawsuit:</strong> After that first victory, the contract's
      condition has been met. Protagoras can sue for the fee.
    </p>
  </Panel>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    A later result cannot retroactively make the unpaid fee due at the start of the first case.
    The ordinary answer distinguishes the contract's condition becoming true <em>after</em> a
    ruling from what was owed <em>before</em> it.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
